# f1 = cachedOf
# `cachedOf` goes by what its callers leave: of `unit` that is 7 or "text", and its guard asks nothing of it. What callers leave is the walk's own word, not Link's: CheckProofsAtRunTime alone believes it.
# RUN(PROOFS): walk f1:ParameterGuard mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# PROOFS: v1: 7|"text" @JSValue
# PROOFS-NOT: CheckProof
# With CheckWalkAtRunTime beside it the guard takes its parameters as if nobody had left anything, and what its callees believe is asked in front of each call.
# RUN(BOTH): walk f1:ParameterGuard mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# BOTH: v1: anything?ParameterOfEscapedFunction @JSValue
# BOTH: CheckProof v1 checkedType=7|"text"
# BOTH: CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# ANSWER: number:5
# ANSWER: string:54!
# ANSWER: string:195!
